# Tauri 2 desktop (Infinity Express)

## Stack

- Shell is **Tauri 2** (not Electron). Frontend is Vite + React under `src/`.
- Rust entry: [`src-tauri/src/lib.rs`](src-tauri/src/lib.rs) via `app_lib::run()`.
- Scripts: `npm run tauri:dev` / `tauri:build`. Browser-only: `npm run dev`.

## Plugins in use

Registered on the builder in `lib.rs`:

- `tauri-plugin-dialog` → `@tauri-apps/plugin-dialog`
- `tauri-plugin-fs` → `@tauri-apps/plugin-fs`

NPM also has `@tauri-apps/api` (e.g. `isTauri()`).

Capabilities: [`src-tauri/capabilities/default.json`](src-tauri/capabilities/default.json)

- `core:default`
- `dialog:default` (open + save)
- `fs:allow-write-text-file`

Dialog-selected paths are **auto-scoped for the session**, so `writeTextFile` on a path returned by `save()` does not need a broad FS allow-list. Scope is not persisted across app restarts.

## Frontend helpers

Prefer extending [`src/lib/desktop/fsDialogs.ts`](src/lib/desktop/fsDialogs.ts) over scattering plugin imports:

| Helper | Behavior |
| --- | --- |
| `isDesktopApp()` | `isTauri()` from `@tauri-apps/api/core` |
| `saveTextFile(name, contents)` | `save({ defaultPath, filters })` then `writeTextFile`; `false` if cancelled |
| `pickDirectory(title?)` | `open({ directory: true, multiple: false })`; `null` if cancelled or not Tauri |

### Call sites

- **Export Save** ([`ExportDialog.tsx`](src/ui/ExportDialog.tsx)): desktop → `saveTextFile`; browser → `downloadText` Blob fallback.
- **Engine Browse** ([`EngineStation.tsx`](src/ui/EngineStation.tsx)): `pickDirectory`; paths persist via [`gameFolderPrefs.ts`](src/lib/ui/gameFolderPrefs.ts) (`infinity-express.game-folders` in localStorage).

## Prefs vs native storage

Plain string prefs (game folders, chrome, detail pane, mods catalog) use **localStorage** helpers under `src/lib/ui/`. Do **not** add `tauri-plugin-store` unless persistence must live outside the webview.

## Adding more native FS

1. Cargo + npm plugin (if new).
2. `.plugin(...::init())` in `lib.rs`.
3. Capability permission in `default.json`.
4. Thin wrapper in `src/lib/desktop/`; keep browser fallbacks when useful.

